<title>HONG KONG: Lane Crawford posts interim net loss.</title>
<headline>Lane Crawford posts interim net loss.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings per A Shr (H.K. cents) 80.3 loss vs 23.4 gain</p>
<p>Earnings per B Shr (H.K. cents) 8.0 loss  vs 2.3 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend A shr (H.K. cents)     17.0	vs 20.0</p>
<p>    Dividend B shr (H.K. cents)     1.5	 vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		   33.7 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net				     90.8 loss vs 26.4 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover				880.3     vs 855.8</p>
<p>    Company name			  Lane Crawford International</p>
<p>						Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close			   January 14-17, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable		    January 28, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Lane Crawford International is engaged in investment holding, retailing, trading and property investment.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss due mainly to the cost of closing down the store operation in Singapore and closing down the Lane Crawford Express operations.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
